Feature: Transfer active files from Vendor S3 bucket to Purgo S3 folder based on configuration in ingest_config_master

  As a data engineer,
  I want a Databricks PySpark script to transfer files from the vendor's S3 bucket to the Purgo S3 folder,
  ensuring only active files are ingested and files already present in Purgo or Archive are not duplicated,
  using S3 paths and flags from the authoritative ingest_config_master table.

  Background:
    Given the Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" contains valid "access_key" and "secret_key"
    And the Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks" and schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the authoritative configuration table is "purgo_playground.ingest_config_master"
    And the script retrieves S3 paths from columns "s3_vendor_path", "s3_landing_path", and "s3_archive_path"
    And the script processes all configs in "ingest_config_master" where "active_flag" = "A"
    And "file name" refers to the base file name (not full S3 key)
    And file matching is by exact file name (case-sensitive)
    And the script processes only files at the root of the Vendor S3 path (no recursion into subfolders)
    And the script performs a copy (not move) operation (files remain in Vendor S3 after transfer)
    And all file types and formats are eligible for transfer
    And if a file with the same name exists in Purgo S3 folder, the file is skipped (not overwritten)
    And the Archive S3 folder is per config, using "s3_archive_path" from the same config row
    And the script logs all transferred files and errors to "purgo_playground.s3_file_process_log" with appropriate status and timestamp

  Scenario Outline: Happy path - Transfer eligible files from Vendor S3 to Purgo S3
    Given a config in ingest_config_master with config_id "<config_id>", active_flag "A", s3_vendor_path "<vendor_path>", s3_landing_path "<purgo_path>", s3_archive_path "<archive_path>"
    And the Vendor S3 folder "<vendor_path>" contains files: <vendor_files>
    And the Purgo S3 folder "<purgo_path>" contains files: <purgo_files>
    And the Archive S3 folder "<archive_path>" contains files: <archive_files>
    When the script is executed
    Then only files in <vendor_files> that are not present in <purgo_files> or <archive_files> are copied to "<purgo_path>"
    And the copied files remain in "<vendor_path>"
    And the copied files are not present in "<archive_path>"
    And the s3_file_process_log table is updated with file_status "SUCCESS" and current timestamp for each transferred file

    Examples:
      | config_id | vendor_path                | purgo_path                 | archive_path               | vendor_files                | purgo_files     | archive_files   |
      | CFG001    | s3://vendor-bucket/folder1 | s3://purgo-bucket/landing1 | s3://purgo-bucket/archive1 | ["file1.csv","file2.csv"]   | []              | []              |
      | CFG002    | s3://vendor-bucket/folder2 | s3://purgo-bucket/landing2 | s3://purgo-bucket/archive2 | ["a.txt","b.txt","c.txt"]   | ["a.txt"]       | ["c.txt"]       |

  Scenario Outline: Error - File already exists in Purgo S3 folder
    Given a config in ingest_config_master with config_id "<config_id>", active_flag "A", s3_vendor_path "<vendor_path>", s3_landing_path "<purgo_path>", s3_archive_path "<archive_path>"
    And the Vendor S3 folder "<vendor_path>" contains files: <vendor_files>
    And the Purgo S3 folder "<purgo_path>" contains files: <purgo_files>
    And the Archive S3 folder "<archive_path>" contains files: []
    When the script is executed
    Then files in <vendor_files> that are already present in <purgo_files> are not copied
    And the s3_file_process_log table is updated with file_status "SKIPPED_EXISTS" and current timestamp for each skipped file

    Examples:
      | config_id | vendor_path                | purgo_path                 | archive_path               | vendor_files                | purgo_files     |
      | CFG003    | s3://vendor-bucket/folder3 | s3://purgo-bucket/landing3 | s3://purgo-bucket/archive3 | ["file1.csv","file2.csv"]   | ["file1.csv"]   |

  Scenario Outline: Error - File already exists in Archive S3 folder
    Given a config in ingest_config_master with config_id "<config_id>", active_flag "A", s3_vendor_path "<vendor_path>", s3_landing_path "<purgo_path>", s3_archive_path "<archive_path>"
    And the Vendor S3 folder "<vendor_path>" contains files: <vendor_files>
    And the Purgo S3 folder "<purgo_path>" contains files: []
    And the Archive S3 folder "<archive_path>" contains files: <archive_files>
    When the script is executed
    Then files in <vendor_files> that are already present in <archive_files> are not copied
    And the s3_file_process_log table is updated with file_status "SKIPPED_ARCHIVE" and current timestamp for each skipped file

    Examples:
      | config_id | vendor_path                | purgo_path                 | archive_path               | vendor_files                | archive_files   |
      | CFG004    | s3://vendor-bucket/folder4 | s3://purgo-bucket/landing4 | s3://purgo-bucket/archive4 | ["file1.csv","file2.csv"]   | ["file2.csv"]   |

  Scenario: Error - No active configs in ingest_config_master
    Given there are no rows in ingest_config_master with active_flag "A"
    When the script is executed
    Then no files are transferred
    And the script logs "No active configs found" with file_status "ERROR" in s3_file_process_log

  Scenario Outline: Error - S3 path missing in config
    Given a config in ingest_config_master with config_id "<config_id>", active_flag "A", s3_vendor_path "<vendor_path>", s3_landing_path "<purgo_path>", s3_archive_path "<archive_path>"
    When the script is executed
    Then if any of <vendor_path>, <purgo_path>, or <archive_path> is null or empty, the script logs "Missing S3 path in config" with file_status "ERROR" in s3_file_process_log for config_id "<config_id>"
    And no files are transferred for that config

    Examples:
      | config_id | vendor_path                | purgo_path                 | archive_path               |
      | CFG005    |                            | s3://purgo-bucket/landing5 | s3://purgo-bucket/archive5 |
      | CFG006    | s3://vendor-bucket/folder6 |                            | s3://purgo-bucket/archive6 |
      | CFG007    | s3://vendor-bucket/folder7 | s3://purgo-bucket/landing7 |                            |

  Scenario Outline: Error - AWS credentials missing or invalid
    Given the Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" does not contain valid "access_key" or "secret_key"
    When the script is executed
    Then the script logs "AWS credentials missing or invalid" with file_status "ERROR" in s3_file_process_log for all attempted configs
    And no files are transferred

    Examples:
      | config_id |
      | CFG008    |

  Scenario Outline: Error - S3 access denied or path not found
    Given a config in ingest_config_master with config_id "<config_id>", active_flag "A", s3_vendor_path "<vendor_path>", s3_landing_path "<purgo_path>", s3_archive_path "<archive_path>"
    And the S3 path "<error_path>" is inaccessible or does not exist
    When the script is executed
    Then the script logs "S3 access denied or path not found: <error_path>" with file_status "ERROR" in s3_file_process_log for config_id "<config_id>"
    And no files are transferred for that config

    Examples:
      | config_id | vendor_path                | purgo_path                 | archive_path               | error_path                  |
      | CFG009    | s3://vendor-bucket/folder9 | s3://purgo-bucket/landing9 | s3://purgo-bucket/archive9 | s3://vendor-bucket/folder9  |
      | CFG010    | s3://vendor-bucket/folder10| s3://purgo-bucket/landing10| s3://purgo-bucket/archive10| s3://purgo-bucket/landing10 |

  Scenario: Validation - Only configs with active_flag "A" are processed
    Given ingest_config_master contains configs with active_flag values "A", "I", and "D"
    When the script is executed
    Then only configs with active_flag "A" are processed for file transfer
    And configs with active_flag "I" or "D" are ignored

  Scenario: Validation - File names are matched by base name only
    Given the Vendor S3 folder contains files "subdir/file1.csv" and "file2.csv"
    And the Purgo S3 folder contains "file1.csv"
    When the script is executed
    Then "file1.csv" is considered present in Purgo S3 and is not copied, regardless of subfolder in Vendor S3
    And "file2.csv" is copied if not present in Purgo or Archive

  Scenario: Logging - All file transfer attempts are logged
    Given a file transfer attempt is made for "file3.csv"
    When the transfer is successful
    Then s3_file_process_log contains an entry with file_name "file3.csv", file_status "SUCCESS", and the correct S3 paths and timestamp

  Scenario: Logging - All skipped or error files are logged
    Given a file transfer attempt is skipped or fails for "file4.csv"
    When the transfer is skipped due to existing file or error
    Then s3_file_process_log contains an entry with file_name "file4.csv", file_status "SKIPPED_EXISTS", "SKIPPED_ARCHIVE", or "ERROR" as appropriate, and the correct S3 paths and timestamp

  Scenario: Validation - Files are not processed recursively in subfolders
    Given the Vendor S3 folder contains "file5.csv" and "subdir/file6.csv"
    When the script is executed
    Then only "file5.csv" at the root of the Vendor S3 path is considered for transfer
    And "subdir/file6.csv" is ignored

  Scenario: Validation - All file types are eligible for transfer
    Given the Vendor S3 folder contains "data.csv", "image.png", and "report.pdf"
    When the script is executed
    Then all files not present in Purgo or Archive are eligible for transfer regardless of file extension

  Scenario: Validation - Files are copied, not moved
    Given a file "file7.csv" is copied from Vendor S3 to Purgo S3
    When the script is executed
    Then "file7.csv" remains in the Vendor S3 folder after transfer

  Scenario: Validation - Archive S3 folder is per config
    Given two configs with different s3_archive_path values
    When the script is executed
    Then each config uses its own s3_archive_path for archive file checks

  Scenario: Validation - File name matching is case-sensitive
    Given the Vendor S3 folder contains "File8.csv" and "file8.csv"
    And the Purgo S3 folder contains "file8.csv"
    When the script is executed
    Then "File8.csv" is considered a different file and is eligible for transfer if not present in Archive

  Scenario: Error - No files to transfer
    Given the Vendor S3 folder contains no files not already present in Purgo or Archive
    When the script is executed
    Then no files are transferred
    And the script logs "No eligible files to transfer" with file_status "SKIPPED_NONE" in s3_file_process_log

  Scenario: Error - Unexpected exception during file transfer
    Given a file transfer attempt for "file9.csv" raises an unexpected exception
    When the script is executed
    Then the script logs "Unexpected error: <exception_message>" with file_status "ERROR" in s3_file_process_log for "file9.csv"
